1. Split Ceremony C1 into the exact up-front permission ceremony named by the owner and a later brief macOS system-VPN approval prompt. C1 currently inserts agent build work, review/acceptance, and a signed disposable probe between portal authorization and the VPN prompt, so it is not one short human permission session. Do not claim the user can remain present through producer and independent-review work.
2. Resolve notarization credential custody safely. The source API credential is currently a mode-0600 file while the project invariant is Keychain-only. The plan must store and verify a named notarytool Keychain profile, then define approved migration, secure custody, or removal of the source file without recording or echoing its path, identifiers, or bytes. Correct canonical text that currently implies ready Keychain notarization credentials already exist.
3. Fix Sparkle ordering. Local key generation may happen early, but the generated macOS target, Info.plist, updater integration, and CI appcast workflow do not exist at C1. Separate generation/custody evidence from later public-key insertion and CI signing verification, and restore explicit dependencies to the generated target and updater/release workflow.
4. Replace the 202-task uninterrupted-autonomy claim with honest holds or explicit owner defaults. TASK-260715-intsjz, TASK-260715-35nc5m, TASK-260715-2gwfaw, and the remaining human half of TASK-260715-3gkwn0 are product or credential decisions. Physical evidence tasks also need executable macOS-only scope or named hold points.
5. Reconcile canonical board contracts, not descriptions alone. ADR-011 still requires physical iPhone evidence. STORY-260716-2m2tl1 and Apple provisioning containers still describe iPhone gates. TASK-260715-3jloqy AC still requires all four App IDs and iPhone profiles; TASK-260715-2ayxqn AC still requires both physical devices; TASK-260715-1u2vpc still includes a Gate-P0 iPhone provider smoke; TASK-260715-3f4rhy still requires both platforms and blocks macOS H2; several M3 physical tasks still require iPhone and Mac. Re-scope these exact AC/scope/container statements or move them to the deferred branch.
6. Keep NIOSSH evidence without scheduling new fork work. TASK-260715-1af33i is unblocked and appears in Wave 1 even though ADR-014 and the owner decision say no further NIOSSH fork work. Defer it explicitly and ensure no scheduler can treat it as part of the working-client path. Comparative evidence may remain without gating libssh2.
7. Repair the serial plan after those changes. Sparkle and C1 dependency removals currently make downstream integration look complete too early, and the wave plan includes human decisions and iPhone-bearing tasks. Regenerate the longest safe macOS autonomous path from the live task DAG and list every later human prompt separately.
8. Align the authoritative goal ledger or document the parent-owned update. `task-board goal get` returned no active primary goal even though the task AC requires canonical goal alignment. A spawned reviewer cannot author the parent goal; the commit-owning orchestrator must update it if the ledger is in scope.

Mechanical validity is necessary but not sufficient here. The current plan would start prohibited NIOSSH work, encounter undeclared human decisions, and eventually require deferred iPhone evidence while claiming a macOS-only autonomous path.
