LOGBOOK.md:540:### 1200 — Bounded libssh2 observation fork clears the remaining public-API clauses (TASK-260720-2sltje)
LOGBOOK.md:541:- DECISION: The existing libssh2 patch remains a single allowlisted six-file delta. It adds typed server-initiated KEX `STARTED`/`SUCCEEDED`/`FAILED` observation with a monotonic generation and one bounded, nonblocking reply-correlated global-request operation; packet ordering, encryption, MAC, KEX algorithms, and crypto implementations remain unchanged.
LOGBOOK.md:542:- DECISION: A timed-out global request stays outstanding until its late reply is drained. This deliberately prevents an unnumbered SSH `REQUEST_SUCCESS`/`REQUEST_FAILURE` from being miscorrelated with a newer request; callers can record a miss at `LIBSSH2_ERROR_TIMEOUT` and continue the same operation to restore the request slot.
LOGBOOK.md:544:- ANOMALY: The broader pre-existing HEV Apple matrix stops before any Xcode build because `HevSocks5Tunnel.xcframework` contains macOS 10.14 and 11.0 object minima while its manifest requires only 10.14. This artifact is outside the libssh2 delta; the task-specific XCFramework inspection and required `make validate-core` gates pass.
LOGBOOK.md:546:### 1145 — libssh2 adapter remains blocked on server-rekey observability and keepalive replies (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
LOGBOOK.md:547:- BLOCKER: The accepted `libssh2_session_rekey` fork clears client byte/time/manual trigger initiation only. The exact public header exports no KEX lifecycle callback or generation query. Pinned libssh2 handles inbound `SSH_MSG_KEXINIT` entirely inside private `packet.c`/`transport.c` state, so the adapter cannot truthfully emit `.serverInitiated`, mark `activeKeyExchange`, increment generation, or distinguish server-KEX success/failure through the public boundary.
LOGBOOK.md:548:- BLOCKER: `libssh2_keepalive_send` writes `keepalive@libssh2.org` with `want_reply=1` but returns after queueing and stores no outstanding request or reply outcome. The public API exposes no generic reply-requiring global request or request-success/failure correlation. Consequently the adapter cannot measure reply RTT, enforce reply timeout/miss allowance, or distinguish acknowledgement from silence.
LOGBOOK.md:549:- EVIDENCE: The public macOS XCFramework exports only `libssh2_session_rekey`, `libssh2_keepalive_config`, and `libssh2_keepalive_send` among relevant symbols. `keepalive.c:52-96` contains no reply wait/state; inbound server rekey is private at `packet.c:1336-1369` and `transport.c:407-425,1039-1048`. Trace callbacks are unavailable in non-debug builds and are not a supported protocol API.
LOGBOOK.md:550:- ROUTING: Do not report these gates green or build a mock-only partial adapter. Recommend a separately reviewed minimal fork extension exposing typed server-KEX lifecycle plus a nonblocking reply-correlated global-request/keepalive API; alternatives are explicitly failing the libssh2 candidate or revising the mandatory contract. Exact options and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_server-rekey-keepalive-blocker.md`.
