blocks:["TASK-260715-3gkwn0"]
scope:In scope: interactive notarytool store-credentials into a named login-Keychain profile; a read-only notary history/whoami style authentication check through that profile alone; recording the profile name, the fact a profile exists, the authenticating team, and the check outcome; an explicit written disposition for the source .p8 file chosen from Keychain-backed migration, retention under a named custodian with documented access control, or secure destruction; a repeatable rotation and revocation procedure keyed to the profile name; shell-history and command-echo suppression for the ceremony commands. Out of scope: recording or transmitting the source file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes anywhere; submitting a real notarization of a product artifact; configuring CI notarization secrets (TASK-260715-3gkwn0 owns the separately-scoped CI credential); Developer ID certificate issuance; iOS or App Store Connect distribution credentials.
ac:1. A named notarytool credential profile exists in the login Keychain and a read-only authentication check succeeds using only that profile name, with the command transcript showing no secret value. 2. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records the profile name, the authenticating team identifier, the check outcome, the date, and the rotation/revocation procedure; it records no file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes. 3. The source App Store Connect API private-key file has one recorded, owner-approved disposition — Keychain-backed migration, retention under a named custodian with documented access control, or secure destruction — with the chosen option and its verification stated explicitly. 4. Shell history and command echo are suppressed for every ceremony command, and a post-ceremony scan of the repository, board resources, shell history, and run logs finds no notarization secret material. 5. If the human declines any step or the credential fails to authenticate, the task records the exact blocking input needed and remains blocked rather than reporting a ready notarization path.
notes:GAP JUSTIFICATION (created 2026-07-28 by TASK-260728-3a2dnr).\nSpec requirement it serves: .spec/goal-macos-v1.md invariant "secrets only in the Keychain — never in providerConfiguration, logs, shell commands, or board resources", and ADR-025.\nThe gap: the owner readiness record states the notarization credential exists as a mode-0600 .p8 file. No existing board element owned bringing it into the Keychain-only form the invariant demands. TASK-260715-3gkwn0 owns the CI release environment, not local credential custody, and its AC assumes a usable credential already exists.\nOut-of-scope check before creation: searched STORY-260716-2byjks and STORY-260716-2m2tl1 for an existing notarization-custody task - none. 3gkwn0 explicitly scopes out local Keychain custody. No duplicate created.\nIndependent review focus item 2 required exactly this resolution.

